  "about": "Inputs and expected results for the plugin-section spelling fold. canonical lists the declared section names per kind, standing in for the names ASH declares. targets are [kind, input, expected] triples, as the data block's spelling vectors are: expected is the declared name the input is a spelling of, or null. sections are whole mappings of one kind: keys in file order, and either the sorted keys left after the fold or, when two spellings of one plugin collide, the first and second key and the declared name. A Python test checks every expected value against ASH's own fold, with the declared names replaced by canonical. A node test checks the JavaScript port against the same file.",
